## Output (JSON only)

```json
{
  "annotated_findings": [
    {
      "id": "KS-NN | RA-NN | UI-NN",
      "current_function": "the operator's current supported function, or 'unknown'",
      "authority_status": "supported|revoked|deprecated|not_adjudicated",
      "retire": false,
      "user_visible_loss": "what the user loses if the behavior is deleted",
      "nondivergent_route": "nearest upstream or kask-owned route + maintenance cost",
      "statement_class": "IS|OUGHT",
      "provenance_tier": "Core|Dual-Axis|Domain Supplement",
      "constraint_force": "blocking|directing|enabling",
      "deletion_test": "complexity_reappears|complexity_vanishes|unclear|n/a",
      "feedback_loop_verdict": "closed|broken|n/a",
      "good_regulator_ok": true,
      "remediation": "..."
    }
  ]
}
```

One entry per finding, keyed by that finding's `id`. `authority_status` MUST
be exactly one of: supported, revoked, deprecated, not_adjudicated, and
`retire` MUST be `true` when it is revoked or deprecated (Gate FA checks
both, and that every finding has an entry). `constraint_force` MUST be exactly
one of: blocking, directing, enabling. `deletion_test` MUST be exactly one of:
complexity_reappears, complexity_vanishes, unclear, n/a. Do not fabricate
adjudication — if a lens does not apply, use `"n/a"` and state why in the
remediation field.
